# Line endings and binary files, the same on every operating system.
#
# Text files are LF in the repository and in the working tree, also on Windows
# (Git for Windows would otherwise check them out with CRLF, its default
# core.autocrlf=true). The bytes matter here: the knowledge retrieval hashes
# its texts and data files, tests compare generated files with committed ones,
# and run.sh / tools/setup_parser.sh do not run with CRLF line endings.
# Python, Node, Java, PowerShell and current editors on Windows read LF files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF. Stored and checked
# out byte for byte (the Gradle wrapper's script is committed with CRLF).
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Binary: never converted, never diffed or merged as text.
*.jar binary
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.gz binary
*.bz2 binary
*.zst binary
*.dem binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# Vendored, minified libraries: text with LF like everything else (they are
# served as they are), but a diff of them is noise.
frontend/static/vendor/** -diff
